{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require flashing lights on street signs when Vehicle Entry Restriction is active",
        "additional_details": "We believe the information on signage at junctions to Restricted Hours Entry streets is hard to absorb at a glance and often too small to read until close. Each of these streets currently has its own rules on entry times, requiring drivers to read and take in the details each time. If approaching at around the time of the restrictions, they also need to check the time. Drivers unfamiliar with an area who enter by mistake risk being caught on camera and fined by the council. Users of streets intended to be safer are at risk from wrongful car entry. We believe that flashing lights on signage will help make roads safer.",
        "background": "We want statutory guidance to require a flashing red light on road signage, warning drivers from a distance that entry to Restricted Hours Entry streets is prohibited. Evasive action could then be taken before inadvertently entering, compromising safety and breaking the law.",
